;; Each missing var is either :jvm-bound (intentionally absent:
;; JVM compiler, classloader, or Java-type machinery a host-free
;; runtime cannot honor) or :gap (genuinely missing portable
;; surface, a real coverage target).
;;
;; The :jvm-bound verdict is cross-referenced from mino's own
;; jvm-only set in tests/clojure_coverage_test.clj (ADR 19:
;; census is the source of truth; mino's jvm-only is what makes
;; a missing var intentional, not a gap). Regenerate after a
;; Clojure baseline move or when mino adds a var:
;;   bb scripts/gen_missing_reasons.bb
;;
;; The dashboard rendering consumes this to split the parity gap
;; into intentional and gap so the number stays interpretable.
